Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_GRANULE=<pages>: the guard takes the whole granule of each page it guessed; default 1 (off)

T91, batch t91-a (door walk): EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD=3 left no glitch moment in 2 of 2 runs (the
control had 2) with the fade in order in both, at 17.1 / 18.1 fps against 17.4. What stayed:
the first frame after the cut to Link's house was over-bright in 1 of 2. That frame reads pages
no frame before it read, so the guess from the last three frames cannot hold them; the game's
per-frame memory goes on from where the last frame's ended, so the pages next to the guessed
ones are the likely ones. With a granule of n pages the guard takes all n pages around each
guessed page. More pages are trapped (arming takes longer) and a write to any of them is copied.

---
diff --git a/src/video_core/ahead_guard.h b/src/video_core/ahead_guard.h
index 21048d9..8bf3ccb 100644
--- a/src/video_core/ahead_guard.h
+++ b/src/video_core/ahead_guard.h
@@ -68,6 +68,8 @@
 ///                                     blocked (EDEN_UP_OOT_FRAME_WAIT), so nothing a held writer
 ///                                     does is needed for the fence.
 ///   EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_COPY_PAGES=<n> the copy pool in pages (default 2048 = 8 MiB, 64 to 16384)
+///   EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_GRANULE=<n>   the guard takes the whole n-page granule of each page it
+///                                     guessed (a power of two; default 1: the page alone)
 /// Covered: buffer uploads, streamed uniform blocks, and the texture handles and storage buffer
 /// pointers read from constant buffers at a draw (ReadGpu). Not covered: texture data and
 /// descriptor tables the texture cache reads.
@@ -133,6 +135,26 @@ inline bool GpuEscape() {
     return on;
 }
 
+/// EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_GRANULE=<pages> (a power of two up to 1024; default 1): the guard takes
+/// the whole granule of each page it guessed, so the pages next to those the last frames read
+/// are in it too. T91, batch t91-a: with =3 no glitch was left on the door walk, but the first
+/// frame after the cut to Link's house was still over-bright in 1 of 2 runs: that frame reads
+/// pages no frame before it read, and the game's per-frame memory goes on from where the last
+/// frame's ended.
+inline u32 Granule() {
+    static const u32 pages = [] {
+        const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_GRANULE");
+        const unsigned long parsed = value != nullptr ? std::strtoul(value, nullptr, 10) : 1UL;
+        const unsigned long clamped = (std::clamp)(parsed, 1UL, 1024UL);
+        unsigned long power = 1;
+        while (power * 2 <= clamped) {
+            power *= 2;
+        }
+        return static_cast<u32>(power);
+    }();
+    return pages;
+}
+
 inline u32 CopyCapacity() {
     static const u32 pages = [] {
         const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_COPY_PAGES");
@@ -425,6 +447,23 @@ void AtPresent(u64 number, u32 fence_id, u32 fence_value, bool previous_reached,
                 }
                 std::sort(pages.begin(), pages.end());
                 pages.erase(std::unique(pages.begin(), pages.end()), pages.end());
+                if (const u32 granule = Granule(); granule > 1 && !pages.empty()) {
+                    // The whole granule of each page: sorted pages give sorted granules.
+                    std::vector<u32> wide;
+                    wide.reserve(pages.size() * 2);
+                    u32 done = ~u32{0};
+                    for (const u32 page : pages) {
+                        const u32 first = page & ~(granule - 1);
+                        if (first == done) {
+                            continue;
+                        }
+                        done = first;
+                        for (u32 at = first; at < first + granule && at < PageLimit; ++at) {
+                            wide.push_back(at);
+                        }
+                    }
+                    pages.swap(wide);
+                }
                 if (!pages.empty()) {
                     std::vector<State::Run> runs;
                     Detail::RunsOf(pages, runs, [](u32) { return true; });
